{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ApwpJQdYRhbHqYvbuhyBon","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved B06.1 = no. Next: B06.2 — When the action runs, the gate rejects it if the instance, operation, target, or arguments differ from the approval, or if the approval has expired.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where an approved action executes. 2) Check the code compares instance, operation, target, and arguments (or hash) against the stored approval and checks expiry at that moment. 3) Answer no if approval is checked only when requested, any field is not compared, arguments are re-read from the model after the check, or expiry is never checked.\nSaved B06.2 = no. Next: B06.3 — Each use of an approval is recorded in one atomic step (single-use or a bounded counter), so replays and parallel calls cannot go past the grant.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where an approval is used or marked consumed. 2) Check it is one atomic step: transaction with lock, compare-and-set, unique constraint, or atomic decrement. 3) Answer no if it reads then writes separately, never marks use, or keeps the count in process memory that parallel workers do not share.\nSaved B06.3 = no. Next: B06.4 — The gate checks that the approver has authority for this action, and rechecks permissions and the relevant resource state when the action runs.\n  How to verify: 1) Find approver checks (role list, `can_approve`, authority mapping). 2) Find rechecks of permissions and resource state at execution. 3) Answer no if any logged-in user can approve, the approver is not checked against the action, or permissions and resource state are not rechecked when the action runs.\nSaved B06.4 = no. Next: B06.5 — If the approval service errors or cannot be reached, the action is denied.\n  How to verify: 1) Find calls to the approval service. 2) Read their error, timeout, and exception handling. 3) Answer no if a `try`/`except` or `catch` logs and proceeds, the default on error or timeout is