{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdrGkz43NYs55xQTSjoQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and saved the result in `agent/brace-findings.json`. The `--batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges` validation passes. I did not run challenges, as instructed. I used normal mode, the specified interpreter, and read-only inspection only.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | gap | `find_valid` (`app/approvals.py:76`) never compares the args hash or the requesting instance. Approvals are never consumed, so replay or changed arguments work for 60 minutes. The approver lookup (`app/main.py:178`) is not scoped to the tenant. The approvals table has no scope column. Approval-service errors do fail closed. |\n| B07 Hard execution budgets | gap | The `count_tokens` call (`app/context_size.py:65`) runs every turn with no metering, and its failures are swallowed. Spend that trips a run limit never reaches the daily user, tenant or fleet quotas (`app/loop.py:151`). Quotas are only checked after the spend. The six limits are set, and sub-agents share the parent budget. |\n| B08 Environment isolation | gap | `deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:75` allows `0.0.0.0/0` on port 443. The ERP rule at lines 58–63 selects a whole namespace. Private ranges and `169.254.0.0/16` are excluded. |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | gap | The same allow-all rule defeats default-deny, and the proxy is only an environment variable. B08 and B09 list each other in `also_affects`. Redirect/resolved-IP checks (B09.3) and block alerting (B09.5) are `unknown` because they live outside this repo. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | needs_evidence | Digest pinning, the keyless signature identity, provenance checks and enforce mode all look right. CI pins cosign v2.6.2. The admission verifier is Kyverno 1.15.2, and its embedded cosign version isn't shown in the repo (B10.5 is `unknown`). |\n\n- **Prescan hits:** I confirmed H002 under B09. I dismissed H001 and H005 with reasons. The other four hits (H003, H004, H006, H007) belong to B11 and R05, which are out of scope for this batch.\n- **For the B05 reviewer:** the ERP `read_prefixes` in `config/policy.yaml` include write operations (`vendor.update_remit_to`, `invoice.mark_paid`, `invoice.void`). These reach the ERP through `erp_call` with no approval. I noted this in the H001 dismissal and did not rate it here, since it belongs to B05.\n- **Extra files:** the run left `brace-prescan.json`, `brace-inventory.json` and `brace-coverage/deviations/attempts-*.json` ledger files in `agent/`. I also edited `scope` in the findings file, which was still a TODO.\n- **Not done:** I didn't write `brace-findings.md`, because that report comes after challenges and merging."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":95018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":560},"output_tokens":787,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35779640-2a0a-46bf-9815-9ff2e081196b","uuid":"55dbe5f0-08ce-4560-907b-ab5858b086f5","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:03:04.079Z","request_id":"req_011CfdrGkhw1R86JdYbV7Mwh"}
